208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 110 0 R
/T (The Movie Ticket Booking System is a database management project developed using MySQL. It is designed to maintain and manage movie information, customer details, show schedules, and ticket bookings in one organised place.)
/E (The Movie Ticket Booking System is a database management project developed using MySQL. It is designed to maintain and manage movie information, customer details, show schedules, and ticket bookings in one organised place.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
209 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 110 0 R
/T (In a cinema, managing movie schedules and booking records manually can be time-consuming and may lead to errors or duplicate records. This system provides an organised way to store, retrieve, update, and manage the information using a relational database.)
/E (In a cinema, managing movie schedules and booking records manually can be time-consuming and may lead to errors or duplicate records. This system provides an organised way to store, retrieve, update, and manage the information using a relational database.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 110 0 R
/T (The project consists of four main tables: Movies, Customers, Shows, and Bookings. These tables are connected using primary keys and foreign keys to maintain relationships and data integrity. For example, a booking cannot be stored for a customer or a show that does not exist. The system also allows users to view booking details, calculate ticket amounts, and generate simple reports using SQL queries. The total amount of a booking is not stored but calculated as the number of tickets multiplied by the ticket price, which avoids storing redundant data.)
/E (The project consists of four main tables: Movies, Customers, Shows, and Bookings. These tables are connected using primary keys and foreign keys to maintain relationships and data integrity. For example, a booking cannot be stored for a customer or a show that does not exist. The system also allows users to view booking details, calculate ticket amounts, and generate simple reports using SQL queries. The total amount of a booking is not stored but calculated as the number of tickets multiplied by the ticket price, which avoids storing redundant data.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
