/Title (The project consists of four main tables: Movies, Customers, Shows, and Bookings. These tables are connected using primary keys and foreign keys to maintain relationships and data integrity. For example, a booking cannot be stored for a customer or a show that does not exist. The system also allows users to view booking details, calculate ticket amounts, and generate simple reports using SQL queries. The total amount of a booking is not stored but calculated as the number of tickets multiplied by the ticket price, which avoids storing redundant data.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1329 0 R
