/Title (A cinema deals with a large number of small, related facts every day: which film is running, at what time, at what price, who bought how many tickets, and how much money was collected. A database management system \(DBMS\) keeps all these facts in a structured form so that they can be searched and combined quickly. Instead of searching through registers, a single SQL query can show every booking of a customer or the total revenue of a day.)
